# Read by GitHub's "Cite this repository" widget, cffconvert and Software Heritage.
#
# Zenodo does NOT read this file: when .zenodo.json is present it is used alone and
# CITATION.cff is ignored entirely. The two must therefore be kept in agreement by
# hand — tests/test_app_version.py asserts that `version` here equals the version the
# code reports, and that .zenodo.json parses.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. An enrichment
  result also rests on the Key Event to pathway mappings produced by the Molecular AOP
  Builder, published separately as 10.5281/zenodo.20184643 — cite that too when you
  report enrichment results.
type: software
title: >-
  Molecular AOP Analyser: Key Event enrichment of gene-expression data against
  molecular Adverse Outcome Pathways
abstract: >-
  A web application for Key Event enrichment analysis of gene-expression data in the
  context of molecular Adverse Outcome Pathways. Offers Fisher's exact test
  (over-representation, both tails) and GSEA (threshold-free, direction-aware), each
  with Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction, and presents results as an interactive
  Cytoscape network of the AOP, a ranked enrichment table, hub genes, an embedded
  WikiPathways diagram and PDF/HTML reports. A batch mode compares up to ten datasets
  across conditions.
authors:
  - family-names: Martens
    given-names: Marvin
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2230-0840
    affiliation: Department of Translational Genomics, Maastricht University
version: 5.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-13'
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/marvinm2/molAOP-analyser
url: https://molaop-analyser.vhp4safety.nl
keywords:
  - adverse outcome pathway
  - AOP
  - Key Event
  - enrichment analysis
  - GSEA
  - transcriptomics
  - toxicology
  - WikiPathways
  - pathway analysis
  - FAIR data
  - new approach methodologies
